---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";

const root = "/temporal-research-agent";
const video = `${root}/demo/out/temporal-literature-review-demo.mp4`;
const poster = `${root}/deck-assets/worker-killed.png`;
---

<PageLayout
  title="Temporal lets us bring a research agent back to life"
  kicker="Temporal case study"
  intro="Improving the durability of our research pipeline using Temporal's Python SDK"
  description="A before-and-after rewrite of a literature-review agent as a durable Temporal Workflow, with code, recorded failure evidence, and implementation notes."
  image={poster}
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="tra stack">
    <nav class="tra__artifacts" aria-label="Project artifacts">
      <a href={`${root}/deck.html`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the deck <span>↗</span></a>
      <a href={`${root}/readme`}>Read the README <span>→</span></a>
      <a href="#code-comparison">Compare the code <span>↓</span></a>
      <a href={`${root}/research-output`}>Read the research output <span>→</span></a>
    </nav>

    <figure class="tra__media">
      <video controls preload="metadata" poster={poster}>
        <source src={video} type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption>
        The Worker dies with two research Activities in flight; Temporal Web
        shows both retries and the completed Workflow.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="tra__premise prose">
      <h2>The original pipeline had already done useful work</h2>
      <p>
        A JavaScript workflow in the
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/code-intelligence-digest">Code Intelligence Digest project</a>
        sent ten research branches through
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/scix-agent">SciX retrieval</a>,
        deep dives, and podcast scripts, then produced two literature reviews.
        One client process held the schedule and inferred progress from files.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Python rewrite gives that progress to a Temporal Workflow. Network
        calls, heartbeats, clock reads, and artifact I/O run as Activities.
        Full evidence stays in an artifact store; Event History carries compact
        IDs, hashes, statuses, and paths.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="code-comparison" class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">The code sample</p>
        <h2>The dependency graph stays recognizable</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tra__code">
        <section>
          <h3>Before source</h3>
          <pre><code>phase('Research')
await pipeline(
  EPS,
  (it) =&gt; agent(/* prompt omitted */, &lbrace;
    label: 'research:' + it.s + '-ep' + it.ep,
    phase: 'Research',
  &rbrace;),
)

phase('Synthesis')
await parallel(literatureReviews)</code></pre>
          <p>Condensed for this page.</p>
          <a href={`${root}/code/before`}>Open the annotated JavaScript source</a>
        </section>
        <section>
          <h3>After source</h3>
          <pre><code>researched = await workflow.execute_activity(
    "research_angle",
    request,
    heartbeat_timeout=timedelta(seconds=30),
    retry_policy=self._retry_policy(review),
)</code></pre>
          <p class="cluster">
            <a href={`${root}/code/workflow`}>Workflow</a>
            <a href={`${root}/code/activities`}>Activities</a>
            <a href={`${root}/code/worker`}>Worker</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section tra__skill">
      <div class="tra__skill-copy">
        <p class="kicker">Beyond the demo</p>
        <h2>The Workflow became an agent skill</h2>
        <p>
          <code>run-durable-research</code> submits a Workflow and returns its
          identifiers. The calling agent can exit. Another agent on the same
          workstation can query progress or retrieve the cited report and
          provenance manifest later.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Workflow owns durable branch state and retry policy. The Temporal
          Service persists Event History and schedules execution. Activities
          perform
          <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/scix-agent">SciX</a>,
          <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/code-intelligence-digest">Code Intelligence Digest</a>,
          artifact I/O, and future model calls.
        </p>
        <a href={`${root}/skills/run-durable-research/SKILL.md`}>Read the skill contract</a>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <button
          class="tra__expand"
          type="button"
          data-expand-image
          aria-label="Expand the completed Workflow screenshot"
        >
          <img
            src={`${root}/deck-assets/workflow-completed.png`}
            alt="Recorded demo frame showing four completed research angles and the replacement Worker identity"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <span>Open full view</span>
        </button>
        <figcaption>Four angles completed under the original Workflow run.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="tra__section">
      <header class="tra__section-head">
        <p class="kicker">Observed recovery</p>
        <h2>Event History records the handoff</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="tra__evidence">
        <figure>
          <button
            class="tra__expand"
            type="button"
            data-expand-image
            aria-label="Expand the Worker failure screenshot"
          >
            <img
              src={`${root}/deck-assets/worker-killed.png`}
              alt="Terminal showing the Worker killed while two Activities are in flight"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <span>Open full view</span>
          </button>
          <figcaption>The Workflow remains open after the Worker receives SIGKILL.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <button
            class="tra__expand"
            type="button"
            data-expand-image
            aria-label="Expand the Temporal Web retry screenshot"
          >
            <img
              src={`${root}/deck-assets/activity-attempt-two.png`}
              alt="Temporal Web showing two research Activities starting on attempt two"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <span>Open full view</span>
          </button>
          <figcaption>Events 7 and 10 show both research Activities on attempt two.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="tra__boundary" aria-labelledby="runtime-boundary">
      <h2 id="runtime-boundary">Runtime boundary</h2>
      <p>
        The source, deck, documents, recording, and captured evidence are
        portable. Running the demo and live research integration is
        workstation-only.
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/scix-agent">SciX</a> and
        <a href="https://www.sjarmak.ai/projects/code-intelligence-digest">Code Intelligence Digest</a>
        depend on local repositories, indexes, databases, services, and Worker
        configuration that are not included here. This page is the
        documentation package; the research service remains local.
      </p>
    </aside>

  </article>

  <dialog id="evidence-viewer" class="tra-viewer" aria-label="Expanded evidence screenshot">
    <button class="tra-viewer__close" type="button" data-close-viewer>
      Close <span aria-hidden="true">×</span>
    </button>
    <figure>
      <img alt="" />
      <figcaption></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </dialog>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  const viewer = document.querySelector<HTMLDialogElement>("#evidence-viewer");
  const viewerImage = viewer?.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>("img");
  const viewerCaption = viewer?.querySelector<HTMLElement>("figcaption");
  const closeButton = viewer?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-close-viewer]");

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-expand-image]").forEach((trigger) => {
    trigger.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const image = trigger.querySelector<HTMLImageElement>("img");
      const caption = trigger.closest("figure")?.querySelector("figcaption");
      if (!viewer || !viewerImage || !viewerCaption || !image) return;

      viewerImage.src = image.currentSrc || image.src;
      viewerImage.alt = image.alt;
      viewerCaption.textContent = caption?.textContent ?? "";
      viewer.showModal();
    });
  });

  closeButton?.addEventListener("click", () => viewer?.close());
  viewer?.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    if (event.target === viewer) viewer.close();
  });
</script>

<style>
  .tra {
    --stack-gap: clamp(var(--space-xl), 8vw, var(--space-3xl));
    padding-block-end: var(--space-3xl);
  }

  .tra__artifacts {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__artifacts a {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 4.5rem;
    padding: var(--space-s);
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-s);
    border-inline-end: var(--border-hairline);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .tra__artifacts a:last-child {
    border-inline-end: 0;
  }

  .tra__artifacts a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    background: var(--color-bg-subtle);
  }

  .tra__media,
  .tra__evidence figure,
  .tra__skill figure {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__media video {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-surface);
  }

  figcaption {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-xs);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .tra__premise {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tra__section {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__section-head {
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .tra__section-head .kicker {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-xs);
  }

  .tra__section-head h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra__section-head > p:last-child {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block-start: var(--space-s);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  .tra__code {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra__code section {
    min-width: 0;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-s);
    border-top: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__code h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .tra__code pre {
    min-height: 15rem;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    padding: var(--space-m);
    overflow: auto;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .tra__skill {
    grid-template-columns: 5fr 7fr;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .tra__skill-copy {
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .tra__skill-copy > * + * {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-m);
  }

  .tra__skill img,
  .tra__evidence img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }

  .tra__expand {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: transparent;
    color: inherit;
    cursor: zoom-in;
  }

  .tra__expand span {
    position: absolute;
    inset: auto var(--space-xs) var(--space-xs) auto;
    padding: 0.35rem 0.55rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-bg) 88%, transparent);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
    line-height: 1;
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(0.25rem);
    transition:
      opacity 160ms ease-out,
      transform 160ms ease-out;
  }

  .tra__expand:hover span,
  .tra__expand:focus-visible span {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }

  .tra__expand:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-accent);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .tra__evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-l);
  }

  .tra-viewer {
    position: fixed;
    width: min(96vw, 96rem);
    max-width: none;
    height: min(94dvh, 60rem);
    max-height: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-m);
    inset: 50% auto auto 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .tra-viewer::backdrop {
    background: oklch(0.12 0.01 70 / 0.84);
  }

  .tra-viewer figure {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
    height: 100%;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .tra-viewer img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 0;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .tra-viewer__close {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 1;
    inset: var(--space-xs) var(--space-xs) auto auto;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    border: var(--border-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--color-bg);
    color: var(--color-text);
    font: inherit;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .tra-viewer__close:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .tra__boundary {
    padding-block: var(--space-l);
    border-block: var(--border-hairline);
  }

  .tra__boundary h2 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-s);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .tra__boundary p {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
  }

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .tra__artifacts,
    .tra__code,
    .tra__skill,
    .tra__evidence {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .tra__artifacts a {
      border-inline-end: 0;
      border-bottom: var(--border-hairline);
    }

    .tra__artifacts a:last-child {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .tra-viewer {
      width: 100vw;
      height: 100dvh;
      padding: var(--space-s);
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
